<title>GREECE: Poseidon, Aspis top Greek fixed-income funds in July.</title>
<headline>Poseidon, Aspis top Greek fixed-income funds in July.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poseidon and Aspis were the top runners among Greece's 39 fixed-income funds in July with year-to-date returns of 19.03 and 13.04 percent, respectively, the association of institutional investors said.</p>
<p>Fixed-income assets under management reached 1.965 trillion drachmas in end-July, up 47.65 percent since the beginning of the year and 1.12 percent on June.</p>
<p>They made up 35.37 percent of the mutual fund industry's total assets, which rose to 5.41 trillion drachmas ($18.5 billion) in end-July, an increase of 4.93 percent on June and 50.8 percent since the start of the year.</p>
